From: C2000MAX maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] fw4: keep EQoS-marked connections out of flowtable

C2000MAX sets a dedicated high-order bit for connections shaped by tc/IFB.
Do not add those connections to the software flowtable, otherwise the fast
forwarding path can bypass the selected queue. Testing one bit preserves
mwan3 and other applications' packet marks.

--- a/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/ruleset.uc
+++ b/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/ruleset.uc
@@ -138,1 +138,1 @@
-		meta l4proto { tcp, udp } flow offload @ft;
+		meta mark & 0x00800000 == 0 meta l4proto { tcp, udp } flow offload @ft;
